  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Fox Shape",
    "definition_type_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": "Dragon Empires Primer pg. 5",
    "definition_raw": "Source Dragon Empires Primer pg. 5\nYou can change into a fox in addition to your other forms.\n\nPrerequisites: Cha 13, base attack bonus +3, kitsune.\n\nBenefit: You can take the form of a fox (Pathfinder RPG Bestiary 3 112) whose appearance is static and cannot be changed each time you assume this form. Your bite attack’s damage is reduced to 1d3 points of damage on a hit, but you gain a +10 racial bonus on Disguise checks made to appear as a fox. Changing from kitsune to fox shape is a standard action. This ability otherwise functions as beast shape II, and your ability scores change accordingly.",
    "links_raw": [
      {
        "anchor_text_raw": "Dragon Empires Primer pg. 5",
        "href_raw": "http://paizo.com/products/btpy8pg0?Pathfinder-Player-Companion-Dragon-Empires-Primer",
